From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tom Plant <tom@tplant.com.au>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 00:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] riscv: dts: thead: lichee-pi-4a: skip the SDIO 1.8 V switch
 for Wi-Fi

The RTL8723DS I/O rail (VCCIO-WIFI) is wired to VDD_1V8, so the bus
already signals at 1.8 V. The RTL8723DS answers CMD5 and offers S18A,
but the 3.3 V -> 1.8 V switch (CMD11) then fails and every retry ends
in "error -110 whilst initialising SDIO card". With no-1-8-v the card
enumerates. Tested on a Lichee Pi 4A.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/arch/riscv/boot/dts/thead/th1520-lichee-pi-4a.dts
+++ b/arch/riscv/boot/dts/thead/th1520-lichee-pi-4a.dts
@@ -175,6 +175,8 @@
 	cap-sdio-irq;
 	keep-power-in-suspend;
 	mmc-pwrseq = <&wifi_pwrseq>;
+	/* VCCIO-WIFI is fixed at 1.8 V, so there is nothing to switch */
+	no-1-8-v;
 	non-removable;
 	status = "okay";
 };
